            "incomplete": "Reckoner is an Oracle reskin and casts DIVINE, spontaneous, Charisma (author ruling 2026-09-19). Slot/repertoire table above is the PF2e Oracle's, levels 1-2 only (from Archives of Nethys: L1 5 cantrips/3 rank-1 slots/3 known, L2 4 slots/4 known; rank 2 arrives at level 3, ranks then follow the Oracle table). Levels 3-20 still to fill. Author ruling: a slot cast counts as an Overflow draw (first each day free, each later draw advances the Reckoning one stage); cantrips and focus spells also count -- the page does not yet say so. The pf2e-cinderfall-module must be updated before spontaneous divine slots build from this record; until then set them by hand on the sheet. reckoner.html needs the spellcasting stat, table columns and the draw rule (page untouched on purpose).",
            "terms": [
                [
                    "Source",
                    "<strong>The specific vast, indifferent thing you channel</strong> — chosen at 1st level alongside your Aspect, from three options (§3): the Halving, the Singularity, or the Outside. Whichever you pick, the ledger works the same way, and none of the three will ever interfere with a draw (§4). The Halving and the Outside can't — they don't perceive you. The Singularity does, and simply doesn't care to stop you. Only what the erosion looks like changes — plus one track the Singularity carries alone (§5)."
                ],
                [
                    "The Halving",
                    "<strong>The default Source, and the first one anyone catalogued.</strong> Not a being — a cosmic constant, closer to the mathematics of decay than to a character. It was doing what it does before the Turning, before humanity, and will keep doing it after everyone reading this is gone."
                ],
                [
                    "The Litany",
                    "<strong>The action you take to draw Overflow</strong> — your spellcasting, mechanically speaking. In fiction, it's the liturgical method that lets a mortal draw on a Source at all: recitation and ritual mathematics, not conversation. You don't ask. You recite the proof and the overflow comes or it doesn't."
                ],
                [
                    "Overflow",
                    "<strong>Your granted spells and abilities</strong> — what reciting the Litany gives you, and what advances your Reckoning each time you draw one. Not a gift, a byproduct. A drop of something enormous that was always going to happen anyway, caught on the way past."
                ],
                [
                    "Aspect",
                    "<strong>Your subclass, chosen at 1st level</strong> from your Source's four options — grants a feature again at 7th (§3). Which facet of your Source's endless process you've attuned to."
                ],
                [
                    "The Reckoning",
                    "<strong>The fixed, foreseeable cost of channeling</strong> — a four-stage penalty track that rises in known increments as you draw Overflow and resets every morning (§5). Not your Source's wrath, since it has none, but the price of something that scale passing through a body built to last."
                ]
            ],
